# Lower bound -h ≤ ord_P(j) at a cusp place

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.neg_width_le_ord_of_order_eq_mul_ord_of_qExpansion_slash`
(`4093daea-d82a-5454-a50b-37a48e45b108`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `c2314ac3-a44b-5672-9928-2ee3729dcb03`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $\Gamma$ be a finite-index subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ containing the translation $T$
and satisfying `IsCongruenceSubgroup`, and write $N$ for the index of the normal core of $\Gamma$.
Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subset \mathbb Q((q))$ equal to
[`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), i.e. the subfield generated
over $\mathbb Q$ by the quotients of the integral $q$-expansion series attached to pairs of modular
forms of one and the same weight $k$ on $\Gamma$ admitting integral $q$-expansions, with nonzero
denominator series; let $F =$ `laurentBaseChange ℂ F₀` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb C
\subset \mathbb C((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $F_0$. Let $y \in F$ have
underlying Laurent series `jqModC ℂ`, that is $q^{-1}$ times the image of the power series
$E_4^3\cdot(\text{inverse }\eta\text{-unit})$. Let $\sigma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, let $\Phi
\colon F \to \mathbb C((q))$ be a ring homomorphism, let $P$ be a place of $F$ over $\mathbb C$ (a
proper valuation subring containing $\mathbb C$ whose ideals are principal), and let $e$ be a
positive natural number. Assume: (i) compatibility of $\Phi$ with presentations by modular forms,
namely for all $x \in F$, all $k \in \mathbb Z$ and all weight-$k$ modular forms $g,h$ on $\Gamma$
with $h \ne 0$, if $x$ times the width-$1$ $q$-expansion of $h$ equals that of $g$, then $\Phi x$
times the width-$N$ $q$-expansion of $h\mid_k\sigma$ equals the width-$N$ $q$-expansion of
$g\mid_k\sigma$; (ii) $(\Phi x).\mathrm{order} = e\cdot \operatorname{ord}_P(x)$ for every $x \ne
0$; (iii) $(\Phi y).\mathrm{order} = -N$. Then for every positive natural number $h$ with $\sigma
T^h \sigma^{-1} \in \Gamma \sqcup \langle -1\rangle$ one has $-h \le \operatorname{ord}_P(y)$.

This is one half of the computation of the order of the $j$-invariant at the place of the function
field of $X(\Gamma)$ corresponding to the cusp $\sigma\infty$: the bound holds for any period $h$ of
that cusp in $\pm\Gamma$, with no minimality or degree condition imposed. It is used by
[`ModularCurve.ord_eq_neg_width_of_order_eq_mul_ord_of_qExpansion_slash`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_eq_neg_width_of_order_eq_mul_ord_of_qExpansion_slash),
where the matching upper bound turns it into the equality $\operatorname{ord}_P(y) = -h$ for the
exact cusp width.

